# RFC7162. A client has to enable QRESYNC before it may use the select
# parameter. Once it has, an expunge is reported as VANISHED rather
# than EXPUNGE, and on a resync the server sends VANISHED (EARLIER)
# before any FETCH, so the client can map message numbers to UIDs.
depends 20
send 1
a enable qresync
receive 2
* ENABLED QRESYNC
a OK done
send 1
b select inbox (qresync (1 2))
receive 9
* 20 EXISTS
* 20 RECENT
* OK [UIDNEXT 21] next uid
* OK [HIGHESTMODSEQ 2] next modseq - 1
* FLAGS (\Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen)
* OK [PERMANENTFLAGS (\Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen \*)] permanent flags
* OK [UIDVALIDITY 1] uid validity
* OK [MAILBOXID (f...)] stable mailbox ID
b OK [READ-WRITE] done
send 1
c store 4,11 +flags.silent \seen
receive 2
* OK [HIGHESTMODSEQ 3] next modseq - 1
c OK done
send 1
d store 7 +flags.silent \deleted
receive 2
* OK [HIGHESTMODSEQ 4] next modseq - 1
d OK done
send 1
e expunge
receive 3
* OK [HIGHESTMODSEQ 5] next modseq - 1
* VANISHED 7
e OK done
send 1
f select inbox (qresync (1 2))
receive 13
* OK [CLOSED] I, missa est
* 19 EXISTS
* 0 RECENT
* OK [UIDNEXT 21] next uid
* OK [HIGHESTMODSEQ 5] next modseq - 1
* FLAGS (\Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen)
* OK [PERMANENTFLAGS (\Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen \*)] permanent flags
* VANISHED (EARLIER) 7
* 4 FETCH (UID 4 FLAGS (\Seen) MODSEQ (3))
* 10 FETCH (UID 11 FLAGS (\Seen) MODSEQ (3))
* OK [UIDVALIDITY 1] uid validity
* OK [MAILBOXID (f...)] stable mailbox ID
f OK [READ-WRITE] done
end
